=== WHAT THIS PROVES (the Wave-4 WMMA milestone) ===
A WMMA bf16 matmul VARIANT (kernels/generated/matmul_wmma.cu) compiles with hipcc
gfx1101, RUNS on the 7800 XT, and passes assert_correct vs golden (contract C: cosine
>= 0.999 AND max_rel_err <= 1e-2 AND pcc >= 0.99; bf16 RNE in / fp32 accumulate / bf16
RNE out). It is ADDITIVE to the scalar baseline: the tiled scalar matmul
(kernels/generated/matmul.cu, Todo 10) is UNCHANGED and remains the correctness
reference; WMMA is a codegen variant of the CLOSED `polykernel.matmul` op the
autotuner (Todo 25) can SELECT. No new op, no new declared attribute — `path=wmma`
is a report annotation (contract H), not a new op.

=== INSTRUCTION + APPROACH (raw clang builtin, NOT rocWMMA) ===
Uses the RDNA3 `v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_bf16` instruction directly via the clang builtin
    v8f __builtin_amdgcn_wmma_f32_16x16x16_bf16_w32(v16bf a, v16bf b, v8f c);
(raw builtin chosen over rocWMMA: zero extra dependency, full control of the fragment
layout, the same idiom vLLM / llama.cpp ship in production on RDNA3). One wave (32
lanes) computes one 16x16 f32 accumulator tile from 16x16 bf16 A and 16x16 bf16 B:
16 bf16 elems/lane input (v16bf), 8 f32 elems/lane accumulator (v8f). Fragment types:
    using pk_wmma_a = __bf16 __attribute__((ext_vector_type(16)));
    using pk_wmma_c = float  __attribute__((ext_vector_type(8)));

FRAGMENT LANE-MAPPING (RDNA3 wave32; validated bit-exact against production RDNA3 WMMA
— AMD GPUOpen "WMMA on RDNA3" layout; cross-checked vs Avarok/atlas strix-hip GEMMs
"validated bit-exact" and ggml/llama.cpp mma.cuh RDNA3 path):
    A load (MxK row-major): lane l -> a[i] = A_tile[l & 15][i],  i = 0..15 (full K-row)
    B load (KxN):           lane l -> b[k] = B_tile[k][l & 15],  k = 0..15 (full K-col)
    Store / accumulator:    lane l, elem e (0..7) -> C[2*e + (l >> 4)][l & 15]
Lanes l and l+16 hold the SAME A-row / B-col (inputs duplicated across the two lane
halves); the accumulator INTERLEAVES even rows in lanes 0..15 and odd rows in lanes
16..31 (row = 2*e + (l>>4)), columns = l & 15. (The believable bug — assuming
CONTIGUOUS rows per half, row = 8*(l>>4)+e — is the negative path; see w4_wmma_neg.log.)

pk_bf16 (__hip_bfloat16) fragments are populated by casting through fp32
((__bf16)pk_bf162float(x)) — lossless for bf16-representable values, so the rounding
contract holds: bf16 in, fp32 accumulate (in the WMMA unit), bf16 RNE out.

