=== SHAPES (all multiples of the 16x16x16 WMMA tile — the clean no-tail case the autotuner selects) ===
matmul_wmma:  (128,128)@(128,128) square  |  (256,128)@(128,256) rectangular (M != N)
              |  (192,160)@(160,224) non-square / non-power-of-two multiple (M=192,K=160,N=224)
              |  (256,256)@(256,256) large-K reduction-order class (calibrated ceiling, see below)

max_rel_err CALIBRATION (MIRRORS test_hip_run.py / test_cpu_ref_fused.py): the single-op
gate max_rel_err <= 1e-2 assumes ONE reduction summed in NumPy's order. The WMMA GEMM
accumulates over K in 16-wide tensor-core tiles (a different fp32 summation order), so
at large K (256) an ISOLATED element lands 1 bf16 ULP off at small magnitude (measured
max_rel_err ~1.01e-2) with cosine == pcc == 1.0 and >= 99.99% bit-exact (NOT a bug; a
real bug tanks cosine/pcc toward 0). test_wmma_matmul_large_k_reduction_order documents
this class with the same calibrated ceiling (5e-2) + full_contract=False the committed
scalar test uses; every other WMMA shape (K <= 224) passes the FULL assert_correct.

